<urn:atm:triage:finding/AM4-STALE-ARCHITECTURE-DOC-PEER-PARTITIONS>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AM4-STALE-ARCHITECTURE-DOC-PEER-PARTITIONS" ;
  triage:title "docs/atm-daemon/architecture.md still lists peer_transport.rs and peer_http_adapter as live/pending, with no retirement marker" ;
  triage:description "docs/atm-daemon/architecture.md's V.2 migration-targets list (line 479) names 'peer_transport.rs' with no retirement marker, immediately next to 'local_ipc_transport.rs (retired by AM.3)' which correctly has one. The file does not exist anywhere in crates/ (confirmed by search). Section 3.1.1's 'Accepted daemon-private partitions' (line 548) still lists 'peer_http_adapter' as a current, live partition ('owns HTTP(S) socket/TLS adaptation only'), even though boundaries/atm-daemon/peer-http-adapter.toml was already deleted per docs/plans/phase-al-am-boundary-transition.md's designated AM.4 action, and no peer_http_adapter module/symbol exists in source. This violates the boundary-transition doc's binding pairing rule (manifest and human-readable boundary doc must be updated in the same PR) and is the same defect class already found and fixed in AM.3 (AM3-STALE-DOCS-LEGACY-PATHS / AM3-BOUNDARY-MANIFEST-STALE). Found by arch-qa (ARCH-001). Quality-mgr confirmed directly by reading both cited lines. Note: arch-qa's companion finding ARCH-002 (an out-of-sequence deletion of boundaries/atm-daemon/peer-delivery-coordinator.toml) was investigated separately and found to be mis-attributed -- that manifest was deleted by commit 18f126d3/22ba8f92 ('refactor: delete AK2 peer delivery worker'), an ancient Phase AK commit unrelated to AM.4 or even to Phase AM; not filed as an AM.4 finding. RECHECK (2026-08-10, commit 241eb256): FIXED. Line 479 now reads 'peer_transport.rs (retired by AM.4; legacy source and boundary manifest removed)', matching the local_ipc_transport.rs convention. peer_http_adapter was moved out of the accepted-partitions section into a new historical-only section ('peer_http_adapter (historical AM.4 partition; its boundary manifest is retired)'); peer_recovery (AM.5's remit) was correctly left untouched. Confirmed by quality-mgr's own direct read of the current file." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-am" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "doc-gap" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "file" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-08-10T21:55:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-08-10T21:35:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AM-S4 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-08-10T21:25:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AM4-STALE-ARCHITECTURE-DOC-PEER-PARTITIONS/AM4-QA1-1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AM4-STALE-ARCHITECTURE-DOC-PEER-PARTITIONS/AM4-QA1-2> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "2" .

